This is what you will get when you run `flutter run -d chrome` and resize:

*a) Mobile (< 600px) - Single Column Stacked*
Header, content cards, and footer appear one below another. In Portrait, it forces column layout.
*b) Tablet (600 ≤ width < 1024) - Two-Column Layout*
Content area uses 2 cards side-by-side. Uses a Hamburger Drawer.

> Visual: 2-column grid, chip shows "Tablet Landscape", banner shows "Active Layout: 2 Column"

*c) Desktop (width ≥ 1024) - Three-Column + Side Navigation Rail*
Shows extended `NavigationRail` on left instead of drawer. Content uses 3 cards per row.

> Visual: Left rail with Dashboard/Analytics/Settings, 3-column grid, chip shows "Desktop"

*Orientation Handling:*
Rotate phone / emulator (Ctrl + Left/Right Arrow in emulator). The `OrientationBuilder` rebuilds and label changes from `Mobile Portrait` to `Mobile Landscape`.

